      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Item</th>
          <th>Question</th>
          <th>Tip</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Item"><strong>Commute and timings</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What are working hours and transport arrangements?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Visit the route at the relevant time</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Item"><strong>Shift and travel rules</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">Are late shifts and travel optional?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Get policy in writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Item"><strong>Complaint process</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">Is there a clear route for harassment complaints?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Ask about the internal committee</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Item"><strong>Culture</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">How do current employees describe it?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Speak to two women there</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Item"><strong>Leave and flexibility</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What leave rules apply?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Read the policy</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Rules protect people, but culture decides how rules work in practice. Ask for both.
  </p>
  <p>
    Trust your instincts if answers feel evasive.
  </p>

